<title>PHILIPPINES: Japan's Itochu to build office building in Manila.</title>
<headline>Japan's Itochu to build office building in Manila.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Itochu Corp said on Thursday it forged a joint venture deal with a local real estate firm to develop a one-billion peso office building in Manila's Makati business district.</p>
<p>Ryosuke Hori, president of Makati Sky Plaza, the joint venture of Itochu and Asian Appraisal Holdings, said in a statement a 30-year old building would be pulled down to make way for a 22-storey office building which will host mainly Japanese tenants.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
